# Python Project Standards

- Language: **Python**
- Dependency management: **pyproject.toml** (no setup.py, no requirements.txt)
- Do **not** introduce new dependencies unless explicitly asked

# Clean Code & Zen of Python

- Simple is better than complex; flat is better than nested
- Explicit is better than implicit; readability counts
- Functions should do one thing and be short (<20 lines preferred)
- Use meaningful, descriptive names for variables, functions, classes
- Avoid deep nesting -- return early, use guard clauses
- No dead code, no commented-out code
- Prefer composition over inheritance

# Clean Architecture

- Separate concerns: domain logic, infrastructure, interfaces
- Business logic must not depend on frameworks or I/O
- Use dependency injection over hard-coded dependencies
- Keep modules focused and loosely coupled

# Style

- Follow PEP 8 and PEP 257 (docstrings)
- Use type hints on all function signatures
- Prefer pathlib over os.path
- Use f-strings for string formatting
